"# Section B: Descriptive Statistics\n\nDescriptive statistical analysis was performed on the extracted EMG features to summarize their central tendency, variability, distribution, and potential outliers. For each of the **eight EMG channels**, nine statistical features were extracted, resulting in a total of **72 numerical features** for **3420 recordings**.\n\nThe analysis includes summary statistics, distribution characteristics, and outlier detection to better understand the properties of the extracted feature set before machine learning.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"\n## B.1 Statistical Feature Extraction\n\nFor every EMG channel, the following statistical features were computed:\n\n- Mean\n- Median\n- Standard Deviation\n- Minimum\n- Maximum\n- First Quartile (Q1)\n- Third Quartile (Q3)\n- Skewness\n- Kurtosis\n\nThese statistical descriptors summarize the signal amplitude, variability, shape, and distribution for each recording.\n\n---","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#============================================================\n# Section B.1\n# ============================================================\n\nimport scipy.io as sio\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import skew, kurtosis\n\nfeature_rows = []\n\nfor _, row in metadata_df.iterrows():\n\n    signal = sio.loadmat(row[\"File\"])[\"value\"]      # (8,8000)\n\n    features = {}\n\n    for ch in range(signal.shape[0]):\n\n        x = signal[ch]\n\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Mean\"] = np.mean(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Median\"] = np.median(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Std\"] = np.std(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Min\"] = np.min(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Max\"] = np.max(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Q1\"] = np.percentile(x,25)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Q3\"] = np.percentile(x,75)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Skew\"] = skew(x)\n        features[f\"Ch{ch+1}_Kurtosis\"] = kurtosis(x)\n\n    feature_rows.append(features)\n\nstats_df = pd.DataFrame(feature_rows)\n\nstats_df.head()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-25T21:45:22.390803Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-25T21:45:22.391188Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-25T21:46:50.779817Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-25T21:45:22.391147Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-25T21:46:50.778865Z"}},"outputs":[{"execution_count":106,"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":"   Ch1_Mean  Ch1_Median   Ch1_Std   Ch1_Min   Ch1_Max    Ch1_Q1    Ch1_Q3  \\\n0  0.003812    0.004883  0.032678 -0.205078  0.151367 -0.004883  0.019531   \n1  0.001690    0.004883  0.059973 -0.581055  0.380859 -0.019531  0.029297   \n2  0.000821    0.004883  0.024204 -0.161133  0.087891 -0.009766  0.014648   \n3  0.000375    0.000000  0.035935 -0.180664  0.205078 -0.019531  0.019531   \n4  0.001671    0.004883  0.051290 -0.561523  0.463867 -0.019531  0.024414   \n\n   Ch1_Skew  Ch1_Kurtosis  Ch2_Mean  ...  Ch7_Kurtosis  Ch8_Mean  Ch8_Median  \\\n0 -0.820756      2.739656  0.000029  ...      5.442377  0.004836    0.004883   \n1 -1.373919     14.541531  0.002884  ...     24.896133  0.003006    0.004883   \n2 -0.664821      2.437372  0.002106  ...      2.190040  0.002182    0.004883   \n3 -0.143156      1.489590  0.001536  ...      2.228204  0.001804    0.000000   \n4 -0.715688      9.891586  0.002811  ...     26.991456  0.002959    0.000000   \n\n    Ch8_Std   Ch8_Min   Ch8_Max    Ch8_Q1    Ch8_Q3  Ch8_Skew  Ch8_Kurtosis  \n0  0.043674 -0.361328  0.209961 -0.009766  0.029297 -1.017475      4.851725  \n1  0.091981 -1.127930  0.888672 -0.029297  0.034180 -0.290126     14.089811  \n2  0.072419 -0.317383  0.385742 -0.034180  0.039062 -0.106199      2.008392  \n3  0.048100 -0.278320  0.405273 -0.019531  0.029297 -0.267680      3.352969  \n4  0.087644 -0.659180  0.869141 -0.034180  0.039062  0.042591      6.580203  \n\n[5 rows x 72 columns]","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: